# Planning Hierarchy

* From Idea to Commit
// From: helpers_root/docs/planning/all.plan_work.how_to_guide.md:19 '## Planning Hierarchy'

::: columns
:::: {.column width=60%}
- @Definition@: work flows from abstract to concrete
  - _Idea_: an abstract, unstructured starting point
  - _Project_: clear goals, a scope, outcomes, and a deadline, tracked as a
    GitHub project
  - _Task_: one actionable item, tracked as a GitHub issue
  - _PR_: the unit of review, one or more per task
  - _Commit_: what lands after a human approves the PR

- @Example@: _"What if users could pick their own short codes?"_ is an idea;
  the new features of `shortlink` are the project; `PR_T1` is a PR

- @Key idea@: planning is the work between the idea and the first PR, and it
  decides how many PRs there are and in which order
::::
:::: {.column width=40%}

```graphviz[width=70%]
digraph Hierarchy {
    bgcolor="transparent";
    pad="0.15";
    splines=spline;
    nodesep=0.25;
    ranksep=0.28;
    rankdir=TB;

    node [shape=box, style="rounded,filled", penwidth=1.6,
          fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=11, margin="0.12,0.06",
          height=0.34, width=1.6];
    edge [color="#A3B1C0", penwidth=1.3, arrowhead=vee, arrowsize=0.75];

    // abstract : orange | planned : teal | reviewed : rose | landed : blue

    Idea    [label="Idea",
             fillcolor="#FBEBD4", color="#D9A85F", fontcolor="#6B4517"];
    Project [label="Project",
             fillcolor="#B7DDD0", color="#6FA890", fontcolor="#1F4E39"];
    Task    [label="Task (issue)",
             fillcolor="#B7DDD0", color="#6FA890", fontcolor="#1F4E39"];
    Pr      [label="PR",
             fillcolor="#F6E1E8", color="#D98CA8", fontcolor="#6B2A44"];
    Review  [label="Review",
             fillcolor="#F6E1E8", color="#D98CA8", fontcolor="#6B2A44"];
    Commit  [label="Commit",
             fillcolor="#D3E3F3", color="#7CA6CE", fontcolor="#1F4E79"];

    Idea -> Project -> Task -> Pr -> Review -> Commit;
}
```
label=fig:planning-hierarchy
caption=The planning hierarchy: an idea (orange) becomes planned work (teal), then reviewed PRs (rose), then commits (blue)

::::
:::

* Capturing an Idea
// From: helpers_root/docs/planning/all.plan_work.how_to_guide.md:44 '## Capture an Idea'

- @Goal@: keep track of the work that could be done, with low friction

- @Algorithm@: the life of an idea
  1. Write a note in a shared doc, e.g., a Google Doc in suggestion mode
  2. Leave it there until someone picks it
  3. Turn the picked idea into `research/ideas/<name>.md`
  4. Run `/research_idea.format` to make it follow the idea template

- @Pros@ of a shared doc for raw ideas
  - It is quick to edit, and an idea is too fuzzy for a GitHub issue
  - The team sees each change in suggestion mode
  - A person who is blocked opens the doc and picks a project

- @Remark@: an issue is a task with a scope, and an idea has no scope yet
  - Other homes for an idea: a shared planning note in the repo, or a clearly
    marked exploratory issue

* Four Phases, Four Human Gates
// From: helpers_root/docs/planning/all.plan_work.how_to_guide.md:67 '## From Idea to Merged PR'

::: columns
:::: {.column width=50%}
- @Definition@: _Define_ says what to build, _Plan_ in which order, _Build_
  ships one reviewed PR at a time, and _Close_ updates the docs

- @Remark@: the agent drafts the output of each phase, and a human approves
  it before the next phase starts

- @Key idea@: run a skill, read its output, fix it, and only then move on: an
  agent never crosses a gate alone
::::
:::: {.column width=50%}

```graphviz[width=55%]
digraph Phases {
    bgcolor="transparent";
    pad="0.15";
    splines=spline;
    nodesep=0.30;
